Every line in the second row is by Nguyễn Thế Huy. The first row is what
survives of the tree the earlier table measured, and the upstream lines are
all inside it; the exact share cannot be restated, because that table was
taken over a narrower selection of files than this one. The tree has grown
by about 8% since the squash, so the upstream share of the whole is now a
little under the quarter recorded above.

Later work in this repository is by Nguyễn Thế Huy: the Browzy rebrand, file
attachments, effort control, prompt enhancement, the slash-dispatch and
session-skills plugin mechanism, provider profile handling and the
installers, and — since the squash — the design-mode element picker,
consumption of page-declared WebMCP tools, in-app skill composition with the
settings redesign, approval gating for send-class calls, per-tab restore of
the last conversation when the side panel reopens, and the tab-group
anchoring for agent-opened tabs.

Bundled third-party fonts
-------------------------

The host package ships DejaVu Sans (regular and bold) through the
`dejavu-fonts-ttf` dependency, used to embed a Unicode font in generated PDF
documents — the PDF standard fonts are WinAnsi-encoded and cannot represent
Vietnamese at all. DejaVu Fonts are released under the DejaVu Fonts License,
a free license derived from the Bitstream Vera Fonts Copyright:

    Fonts are (c) Bitstream (see below). DejaVu changes are in public domain.
    Glyphs imported from Arev fonts are (c) Tavmjong Bah (see below).

The full license text ships with the dependency at
`node_modules/dejavu-fonts-ttf/LICENSE`.
